     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;ve been trying to modify the multivariate probit model in the Stan manual to include a hierarchical intercept that represents site-level effects.  I have been unable to get the model to converge despite trying a number of variations with lengthy run-times and strict control parameters.  <br><br>I believe that part of the issue might be that I am not enforcing a sum-to-zero constraint on the intercept.  The reason for this is that I eventually plan to incorporate spatial autocorrelation among the intercepts (drawing them from a multivariate normal distribution), and I don&#39;t think that either of the sum-to-zero methods described in the manual would work with this.<br><br>Is there some way I could incorporate a hierarchical intercept, or should I just go with hierarchical slopes?  Any assistance would be greatly appreciated.<br><br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">functions </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// This section identical to mvProbit model in manual</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> a</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> s</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        s </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">size</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">a</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>            </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">j </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">size</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">a</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>            s </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> s </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> a</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">j</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#008\">return</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> s</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> D</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">D</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> nPops</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nPops</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> popID</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    real</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> coefScale</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// Standard deviation of alpha &amp; beta; </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#    matrix&lt;lower=0&gt;[nPops, nPops] Dist; // Distance matrix; uncomment for spatial version of model</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>transformed data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>    </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// This section identical to provided mvProbit model </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> N_pos</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n_pos</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">D</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> d_pos</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">size</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n_pos</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> N_neg</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n_neg</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> D</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> size</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n_pos</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">D</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> d_neg</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">size</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n_neg</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> <br>  N_pos </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> size</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n_pos</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  N_neg </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> size</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n_neg</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> j</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    i </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    j </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">d </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">D</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#008\">if</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">d</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>          n_pos</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>          d_pos</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> d</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>          i </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> i </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">else</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>          n_neg</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">j</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>          d_neg</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">j</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> d</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>          j </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> j </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>parameters </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">D</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nPops</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> raw_alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">D</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> raw_beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    cholesky_factor_corr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">D</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> L_Omega</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N_pos</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> z_pos</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N_neg</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> z_neg</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#   real&lt;lower=0&gt; spatialScale;  // uncomment for spatial version</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>transformed parameters </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">D</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> z</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">D</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nPops</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">D</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  <br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">/*    Spatial components<br>    corr_matrix[nPops] Spatial_Sigma;<br>    matrix[nPops,nPops] L_Spatial;<br>    Spatial_Sigma &lt;- exp(-1*Dist/spatialScale);<br>    L_Spatial &lt;- cholesky_decompose(Spatial_Sigma);<br>    for(i in 1:D) alpha[i] &lt;- diag_pre_multiply(rep_vector(coefScale, nPops), L_Spatial) * raw_alpha[i];<br>*/</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// End spatial components</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>   beta </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> raw_beta </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> coefScale</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>   alpha </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> raw_alpha </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> coefScale</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// Non-spatial version</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N_pos</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        z</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n_pos</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> d_pos</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> z_pos</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N_n</span><span style=\"color:#000\">eg</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        z</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n_neg</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> d_neg</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> z_neg</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    to_vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">raw_beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> normal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    to_vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">raw_alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> normal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#    spatialScale ~ normal(0, 1);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>    vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">D</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta_x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>      beta_x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> beta </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> col</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> popID</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    z </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> multi_normal_cholesky</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">beta_x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> L_Omega</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s87pL5U3AwAJ",
   "from": "Bob Carpenter",
   "author": "8aa9b8cc06fdc99c",
   "date": "2015-12-14T19:53:03Z",
   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] Model Consultation: Hierarchical Multivariate Probit",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "I don&#39;t see any reason you couldn&#39;t use hierarchical intercepts\r<br>and slopes.  We typically give those multivariate priors --- see\r<br>the manual chapter on regression.\r<br>\r<br>Identifiability is important, so if it requires a sum-to-zero\r<br>constraint, you need to implement that.  I didn&#39;t understand why\r<br>you thought the method in the manual won&#39;t work.\r<br>\r<br>But before trying to generalize, you want to make sure you can\r<br>fit before the generalization.  Often the problem is with\r<br>identifiability --- hierarchical models are only weakly identifiable\r<br>and often need stronger priors to control the posterior variance.\r<br>\r<br>- Bob\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>\r<br>&gt; On Dec 13, 2015, at 3:50 PM, Christopher Peterson &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">christopher...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; I&#39;ve been trying to modify the multivariate probit model in the Stan manual to include a hierarchical intercept that represents site-level effects.  I have been unable to get the model to converge despite trying a number of variations with lengthy run-times and strict control parameters.  \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; I believe that part of the issue might be that I am not enforcing a sum-to-zero constraint on the intercept.  The reason for this is that I eventually plan to incorporate spatial autocorrelation among the intercepts (drawing them from a multivariate normal distribution), and I don&#39;t think that either of the sum-to-zero methods described in the manual would work with this.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Is there some way I could incorporate a hierarchical intercept, or should I just go with hierarchical slopes?  Any assistance would be greatly appreciated.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; functions {\r<br>&gt;     // This section identical to mvProbit model in manual\r<br>&gt;     int sum(int[,] a) {\r<br>&gt;         int s;\r<br>&gt;         s &lt;- 0;\r<br>&gt;         for (i in 1:size(a))\r<br>&gt;             for (j in 1:size(a[i]))\r<br>&gt;             s &lt;- s + a[i,j];\r<br>&gt;         return s;\r<br>&gt;     }\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; data {\r<br>&gt;     int&lt;lower=1&gt; K;\r<br>&gt;     int&lt;lower=1&gt; D;\r<br>&gt;     int&lt;lower=0&gt; N;\r<br>&gt;     int&lt;lower=0,upper=1&gt; y[N,D];\r<br>&gt;     vector[K] x[N];\r<br>&gt;     int&lt;lower=1&gt; nPops;\r<br>&gt;     int&lt;lower=1,upper=nPops&gt; popID[N];\r<br>&gt;     real&lt;lower=0&gt; coefScale;  // Standard deviation of alpha &amp; beta; \r<br>&gt; #    matrix&lt;lower=0&gt;[nPops, nPops] Dist; // Distance matrix; uncomment for spatial version of model\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; transformed data { \r<br>&gt;     // This section identical to provided mvProbit model \r<br>&gt;   int&lt;lower=0&gt; N_pos;\r<br>&gt;   int&lt;lower=1,upper=N&gt; n_pos[sum(y)];\r<br>&gt;   int&lt;lower=1,upper=D&gt; d_pos[size(n_pos)];\r<br>&gt;   int&lt;lower=0&gt; N_neg;\r<br>&gt;   int&lt;lower=1,upper=N&gt; n_neg[(N * D) - size(n_pos)];\r<br>&gt;   int&lt;lower=1,upper=D&gt; d_neg[size(n_neg)];\r<br>&gt;  \r<br>&gt;   N_pos &lt;- size(n_pos);\r<br>&gt;   N_neg &lt;- size(n_neg);\r<br>&gt;   {\r<br>&gt;     int i;\r<br>&gt;     int j;\r<br>&gt;     i &lt;- 1;\r<br>&gt;     j &lt;- 1;\r<br>&gt;     for (n in 1:N) {\r<br>&gt;       for (d in 1:D) {\r<br>&gt;         if (y[n,d] == 1) {\r<br>&gt;           n_pos[i] &lt;- n;\r<br>&gt;           d_pos[i] &lt;- d;\r<br>&gt;           i &lt;- i + 1;\r<br>&gt;         } else {\r<br>&gt;           n_neg[j] &lt;- n;\r<br>&gt;           d_neg[j] &lt;- d;\r<br>&gt;           j &lt;- j + 1;\r<br>&gt;         }\r<br>&gt;       }\r<br>&gt;     }\r<br>&gt;   }\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; parameters {\r<br>&gt;     matrix[D,nPops] raw_alpha;\r<br>&gt;     matrix[D,K] raw_beta;\r<br>&gt;     cholesky_factor_corr[D] L_Omega;\r<br>&gt;     vector&lt;lower=0&gt;[N_pos] z_pos;\r<br>&gt;     vector&lt;upper=0&gt;[N_neg] z_neg;\r<br>&gt; #   real&lt;lower=0&gt; spatialScale;  // uncomment for spatial version\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; transformed parameters {\r<br>&gt;     vector[D] z[N];\r<br>&gt;     matrix[D,nPops] alpha;\r<br>&gt;     matrix[D,K] beta;  \r<br>&gt; /*    Spatial components\r<br>&gt;     corr_matrix[nPops] Spatial_Sigma;\r<br>&gt;     matrix[nPops,nPops] L_Spatial;\r<br>&gt;     Spatial_Sigma &lt;- exp(-1*Dist/spatialScale);\r<br>&gt;     L_Spatial &lt;- cholesky_decompose(Spatial_Sigma);\r<br>&gt;     for(i in 1:D) alpha[i] &lt;- diag_pre_multiply(rep_vector(coefScale, nPops), L_Spatial) * raw_alpha[i];\r<br>&gt; */ // End spatial components\r<br>&gt;    beta &lt;- raw_beta * coefScale;\r<br>&gt;    alpha &lt;- raw_alpha * coefScale; // Non-spatial version\r<br>&gt;     for (n in 1:N_pos)\r<br>&gt;         z[n_pos[n], d_pos[n]] &lt;- z_pos[n];\r<br>&gt;     for (n in 1:N_neg)\r<br>&gt;         z[n_neg[n], d_neg[n]] &lt;- z_neg[n];\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; model {\r<br>&gt;     to_vector(raw_beta) ~ normal(0, 1);\r<br>&gt;     to_vector(raw_alpha) ~ normal(0, 1);\r<br>&gt; #    spatialScale ~ normal(0, 1);\r<br>&gt;   { \r<br>&gt;     vector[D] beta_x[N];\r<br>&gt;     for (n in 1:N) \r<br>&gt;       beta_x[n] &lt;- beta * x[n] + col(alpha, popID[n]);\r<br>&gt;     z ~ multi_normal_cholesky(beta_x, L_Omega);\r<br>&gt;   }\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "&gt; -- \r<br>&gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Stan users mailing list&quot; group.\r<br>&gt; To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">stan-users+...@googlegroups.com</a>.\r<br>&gt; To post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">stan-...@googlegroups.com</a>.\r<br>&gt; For more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792462947412000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Wn1FEw4LjsEJjkfLoIQxN\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.\r<br>&gt; &lt;probit-multi-hier.stan&gt;&lt;probit-multi-sim.R&gt;\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
